{
  "requirement": "Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through\ntheir `ValidationContext`. The application supplies the configuration under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_agent`. The SDK does not persist it.\nA cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.with_agent`. I did not read `Memory::new`. I assumed it builds a cache without an agent, based on `new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent` and the `NoAgentConfigured` assertion.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. Criteria obtain the agent selected by the domain's validation cache through their `ValidationContext`.\n2. The application supplies the configuration, and the SDK does not persist it.\n3. A cache created without an agent supports deterministic criteria. This is context from the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.deterministic_procedures`.\n\n**Coverage**\n- **Criteria use the cache's agent.**\n  - `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` builds a cache with `ValidationCache::with_agent(OpenAi…)`. It runs `validation::verify` twice against a local HTTP server. It asserts that the configured model, tool set and prompt reach the backend, and that the criterion output is `true`.\n  - `supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat` does the same for Ollama. It also asserts the bearer key, options and tool results.\n  - `agent_executions_isolate_conversations_and_dependency_traces` exercises the agent-based execution path.\n- **The application supplies the configuration, and it is not persisted.**\n  - `bedrock_configuration_attaches_to_a_cache_without_being_persisted` asserts that the cache's `agent` is shared by clones (`Arc::ptr_eq`) and keeps the supplied `config`.\n  - The same test serializes the saved record and asserts it has no `backend` key and does not contain the profile or model strings.\n  - The OpenAI test repeats the check after each `store_evidence`. The saved record must not contain the API key, the model, `backend` or `api_key`.\n- **Backend setup is deferred, and a cache without an agent still runs deterministic criteria.**\n  - `configured_agents_initialize_only_when_asked_and_report_setup_errors` checks `agent.provider.get().is_none()` before any request. A deterministic criterion (`Question(false)`) runs, and the provider is still uninitialized afterwards. Only the awaited ask (`Question(true)`) fails, with `ValidationError::Agent` naming the missing credential variable. This covers \"defers backend setup until a criterion awaits an agent request\".\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` runs a deterministic criterion on a domain whose cache has no agent. It asserts the output and the stored dependency.\n  - `runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls` asserts `NoAgentConfigured` for an ask without an agent, and that nothing is stored.\n  - `new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs` asserts that `ValidationCache::new()` has no agent.\n- `supported_backend_settings_create_transports_without_sending_requests` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs` covers configuration for several backends, although that behaviour belongs to `agent_config`.\n\n**Gaps and exemptions**\n- I found no uncovered obligation, boundary or failure case.\n- I found no marking gaps.\n- No obligation here is delegated to a refining requirement.\n- No {fixme} acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "a7c327df3723dd097da425415d02491ba38f1398e61cad8e250b6b3934e6537e",
